// Plan stage R0z Z9c-B (R-VREF, review round 2, B3 and B4; the bad twin):
// a reference can be live in the window of the task, so the call keeps the
// rule of main. The probe of the review:
// Review probe Z9c-B r2 (B1 with a known capture): `f` gets `&w` as an argument and holds `r` into it while
// the task of its capture `g` pushes to `w` (the closure sees `v` and `w` as separate places).
fn main() / async {
    let w = Vec.new()
    w.push(1)
    let g = || w.push(2)
    let f = |v: &Vec<u64>| { let r = &v[0]; scope { s => s.spawn(g); () }; print(r) }
    f(&w)
}
